      "description": "Watch KVC Westerlo vs Zulte Waregem highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 31, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League took center stage on August 31, 2026 , as KVC Westerlo welcomed Lommel United for a highly anticipated matchup. Both teams entered the pitch looking to establish dominance in a fixture that promised plenty of tactical intrigue. Early Breakthrough at Westerlo The home side didn't take long to find their rhythm, establishing a high tempo right from the kickoff. In the 8th minute, the deadlock was broken when Shunsuke Saito found the back of the net, sending the home crowd into a frenzy. The early goal shifted the momentum heavily in favor of KVC Westerlo , as they continued to press high and disrupt Lommel United's attempts to build from the back. The pressure paid off again in the 25th minute. Anosike Ementa , who was proving to be a constant threat on the wing, provided a brilliant assist for Tobias Hedl . Hedl made no mistake with the finish, doubling the lead and leaving the visitors with a mountain to climb before the halftime whistle even approached. Second Half Dominance and Clinical Finishing As the second half got underway, KVC Westerlo showed no signs of slowing down. Just three minutes after the restart, a foul in the box handed the hosts a golden opportunity. Norman Bassette stepped up to the penalty spot in the 48th minute and calmly converted, further extending the advantage and effectively ending any hopes of a Lommel United comeback. The orchestration of the attack continued to revolve around the partnership between Anosike Ementa and Tobias Hedl . In the 63rd minute, Ementa once again turned provider, delivering his second assist of the match to Hedl . The striker's clinical nature was on full display as he netted his second goal of the evening, putting the game well beyond reach. Closing Stages and Tactical Shifts With the result largely secured, both managers turned to their benches to freshen up their squads. Norman Bassette made way for Isa Sakamoto , while Lommel United introduced Malick Mbaye in an attempt to find a late consolation. The match became more physical in the final ten minutes, resulting in a yellow card for Lasse Floe in the 82nd minute. In the dying embers of the game, KVC Westerlo managed their lead with composure, making late substitutions including Thomas Van den Keybus and David Amegnaglo to see out the clock. When the referee finally blew the whistle after six minutes of added time, the home side celebrated a comprehensive performance that left their opponents searching for answers."
