roduced the likes of Darius Olaru and Rob Schoofs to stabilize the midfield and protect their slim lead. Union SG pushed forward, bringing on Raul Florucz in the 79th minute to spark a late comeback, but the home defense remained resolute. After three minutes of stoppage time, the final whistle blew, confirming a hard-fought victory for St. Truiden in a match defined by swift counter-attacks and individual brilliance."
